# Every local env file. .env.example is committed on purpose and is the only
# one that should ever be: it documents the variables and holds no values.
# STANDING_DEPLOYER_KEY in particular is a spending key and belongs in the
# shell for the length of one command, never in a file in the tree.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.production

# Keys and keystores, in case one is ever dropped here while testing.
*.pem
*.key
keystore.json

.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__
*.pyc
